+        # 2026-07-31 gap-tightening: distbox/speedbox are VERTICAL Boxes with
+        # only two children each (a caption Label + the value-button Grid).
+        # Both were packed with expand=True (pack_start's 2nd arg / the
+        # implicit default used by Box.add()), so any extra vertical space
+        # this grid row is handed by the parent gets split between the
+        # caption label and the button grid -- and since a GtkLabel's own
+        # valign defaults to fill, that extra space renders as blank
+        # padding above/below the "Distance (mm)"/"Speed (mm/s)" text and
+        # around the button row, not anything visually useful. expand=False
+        # on both children, plus vexpand=False on the Box itself, makes each
+        # Box (and this grid row, since nothing else in it still asks for
+        # vexpand) size to its actual natural content height instead.
+        distbox = Gtk.Box(orientation=Gtk.Orientation.VERTICAL, vexpand=False)
